//! Broadcom BTE Bluetooth host stack - Wii Remote platform glue.
//!
//! `main.dol` statically links Broadcom's BTE Bluetooth stack so the game can
//! pair with, and exchange HID reports with, up to four Wii Remotes. This module
//! holds every function translated from that stack so far (the count grows with
//! each pass; the per-wave tables live in `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE*_BT*.md`). It is
//! *platform glue*,
//! not gameplay: if a port replaces the Wii Remote transport with a host API
//! (XInput, keyboard, a PC Bluetooth backend), this whole module becomes dead
//! code. It is kept because it documents what events the rest of the game
//! expected the transport to deliver, and because the globals it owns are part
//! of the original image layout.
//!
//! # Layer map
//!
//! The stack is layered the same way a classic Bluetooth host stack is. Layer
//! names are `// inferred:` from assertion strings in the Ghidra evidence, not
//! from symbols: the shipped image has no symbol table.
//!
//! | Layer | Role | Functions in this module | Original addresses |
//! |---|---|---|---|
//! | HID host (`bta_hh`) | Per-device HID-host state for four remotes: slot allocation, lookup, teardown, disconnect-all, connected count, plus the sixteen-record device-database dump | [`fn_80200000`], [`fn_80200190`], [`fn_8020028c`], [`fn_80200310`], [`fn_80200624`], [`fn_802006e8`], [`fn_8020117c`] | `0x80200000..0x8020117C` |
//! | BTM | Bluetooth device manager: init defaults, two `u16` config globals, the single connection callback, the 16-record device database, connection-slot release | [`fn_80200270`], [`fn_80200cc8`], [`fn_80201094`], [`fn_80201710`], [`fn_8020213c`], [`fn_80202460`], [`fn_80207240`] | `0x80200270..0x80207240` |
