//! - the IPC request service at `0x802243C0..0x802265C0` (17 bodies): the reply
//!   handler and the `0xCD000000` interrupt handler, the request submit, the
//!   kind-1 open and kind-5/6/7 builders, the eight-slot `0xBABE0000` heap
//!   (attach, allocate, free), the two 32-slot tables, the second-arena setup
//!   and the shared completion callback.
//!
//! The IPC block layout is now complete through kind 7: `+0` kind, `+4` status,
//! `+8` id, `+0xC`/`+0x10` first buffer, `+0x14`/`+0x18` second buffer or
//! vector table, `+0x20` callback and `+0x24` callback context. Heap blocks use
//! `0xBABE0000` (free), `0xBABE0001` (allocated) and `0xBABE0002` (alignment
//! pad), with `{magic, payload size, prev, next}` at `-0x10` from the payload.
//!
//! Wave 89 added 26 bodies to the `0x80200000` bucket, all of them in gaps
//! between clusters that waves 66, 79 and 82 had already documented:
//!
//! - the HID-host role-switch completion pair at `0x80200968`/`0x80201320`
//!   (state `+0x11B`, callback byte `+0x11A`, `0x080B` cancel gate),
//! - the BTM RSSI and link-quality request twins at
//!   `0x8020182C`/`0x80201968`, the eSCO packet-type re-selection at
//!   `0x80201D94` and the device-record creator/lookup helpers at
//!   `0x80201FB4..0x802023A8`,
//! - the BTM default block at `0x80202680` and the bring-up retry timer
//!   `0x80202A20`,
//! - the device-ready forwarder `0x80203FE8` and the connectability setter
//!   `0x802045B8`,
//! - the inquiry-result buffer insert/lookup at `0x8020508C..0x80205168` and
//!   the remote-name request gate `0x802058EC`,
//! - the eSCO link-parameter table update `0x802072F8`,
//! - the GAP connection-slot block at `0x8020BCD0..0x8020CA18` (nine bodies):
//!   lookup by CID, the configuration/disconnect callbacks, congestion
//!   notification, the discovery-completion handler and the two remote-name
//!   lookup completions.
//!
//! The GAP cluster uses an eight-record `0x803D43EC` table with `0x60`-byte
//! records (`+0` state, `+1` flags, `+4` handle, `+6` CID, `+9` address,
//! `+0x10` token, `+0x12` result, `+0x14` queue, `+0x20` callback), which the
//! nine bodies now cover end to end.
//!
//! Wave 91 added 29 bodies in two gap runs of the same `0x80200000` bucket:
//!
//! - thirteen HID-host L2CAP event handlers at `0x8021040C..0x80212674`: the
//!   six-entry security registration, the control/interrupt security results,
//!   the control originate, the connect/configuration/disconnect/congestion/data
//!   callbacks and the PSM callback-table registration. They all resolve a
//!   `0x34`-byte record in [`BTM_POOL`] and move it between state `0` (idle),
//!   `1` (originating), `3`/`4` (configured), `5` (disconnecting) and `6`
//!   (awaiting configuration),
//! - sixteen L2CAP/RFCOMM helpers at `0x8021471C..0x8021B648`: the connection
//!   request/complete pair, the four signal builders (connect request/response,
//!   echo, disconnect request), the CCB free-list allocator, the baseband
//!   connect start, the busy-channel test and six RFCOMM port close/window/mux
