/// Builds and queues an HCI vendor command `0xFC00 | opcode`.
///
/// `// observed:` the low opcode byte is `param_2 & 0xFF`, the high byte is
/// `(param_2 >> 8) | 0xFC`, the tag is `len + 3` and the parameter length is
/// `len`. The payload is copied verbatim from `src`.
///
/// `// unknown:` the command family; Ghidra drops the queue argument, so the
/// buffer is passed explicitly (same inference as the wave-5 builders).
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_8020F254`, `0x8020F254`, 244 bytes
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/8020f254_FUN_8020f254.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `buf`: command buffer with at least `len + 0x0B` writable bytes.
/// - `opcode`: low 10 bits of the vendor opcode.
/// - `len`: parameter length; only a positive value copies bytes.
/// - `src`: parameter bytes.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Writes the packet and calls [`fn_8020ac78`].
///
/// # Safety
/// `buf` and `src` must satisfy the sizes above for a positive `len`.
///
/// # Confidence
/// medium - the layout is explicit; the vendor opcode name is unknown.
