/// Sends an L2CAP disconnect request for a child channel.
///
/// Increments the owner's request identifier, records it in the child, builds
/// a four-byte request carrying the two channel ids, pushes it on the owner's
/// send queue and starts the signal send.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80217794`, `0x80217794`, 212 bytes
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/80217794_FUN_80217794.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `channel`: child channel block.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Updates `owner + 0x31` and `channel + 0x35`, allocates a buffer, pushes it
/// on `owner + 0x44` and calls [`L2CAP_SIGNAL_SEND`].
