// Wave 68 clusters.
//
// Four contiguous runs that earlier passes left untouched. Each one owns a
// single table, so the field offsets are shared across its whole run:
//
// - `0x80210100..0x8021254C` drives the sixteen `0x34`-byte HID-host device
//   records at [`BTM_POOL`] - the "connection pool" wave 66 cleared in
//   [`fn_8020fdcc`] and gated in [`fn_8020fe10`],
// - `0x8021995C..0x80219F8C` are RFCOMM port helpers that sit next to the
//   already translated port callbacks,
// - `0x8021A1C0..0x8021AAD8` install and service the RFCOMM LCID callback and
//   block tables at `0x803D543C..0x803D5463` and `0x803D5464`,
// - `0x8021EFA4..0x8021FE24` are the SDP service-database record helpers whose
//   address range ends exactly where the wave-60 SDP client code starts
//   (`0x802202D0`).
