/// Notifies every child channel that has a connect-timeout callback.
///
/// Finds the connection block for `handle`, then walks its child list at `+8`.
/// A child is fed event `6` only when its callback table (`+0x30`) has a
/// non-zero connect-timeout entry at `+0x20`.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80214C18` at `0x80214C18` (112 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/80214c18_FUN_80214c18.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `handle`: connection handle (the `u32` at `+0x28`).
///
/// # Returns
/// `1` when the connection was found, `0` otherwise.
///
/// # Side effects
/// May dispatch event `6` once per child channel.
///
/// # Safety
/// The export calls `FUN_80216B34` with no printed argument; the only caller
/// (`0x8020A6C0`) passes the handle, which is why it is restored here. Each
/// child's callback table pointer must be valid or null-free.
