///
/// The connection handle is the low 12 bits of the little-endian `u16` at
/// payload `+8`. A missing connection frees the packet after a trace line. A
/// connection in state `4` clears the packet's `+6` field, pushes it on the
/// channel's `+0x44` queue with [`QUEUE_PUSH_HEAD`], clears the `+0x40` flag and
/// sends the signal; any other state frees the packet.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80215788` at `0x80215788` (220 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/80215788_FUN_80215788.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `packet`: reassembled packet block.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Queues or frees `packet`, emits one optional trace line, writes the channel
/// flag and calls the signal sender.
///
/// # Safety
/// `packet` must be a live buffer with a readable payload header.
