/// Handles an incoming data indication.
///
/// Three paths. Without a direct data callback the frame is queued on the
/// port's receive queue when `+0x40 + len < 0x2EE1` and the window count is
/// below the maximum at `+0xA0`; if `+0x4E` (the EOF character) appears in the
/// payload the status gains bit `1` (`2`). Buffer overflow frees the packet and
/// reports error `2` through [`RFCOMM_DATA_ERROR_8021CD08`]. With a data
/// callback the frame is passed to it directly after
/// [`fn_80219ff4`] accounting.
