/// port's index byte from the channel and, when no other index is in use,
/// either re-arms the channel retry timer with a two-tick timeout or issues DLC
/// command `8` through [`RFCOMM_COMMAND_8021AAF4`] depending on the resume flag
/// at `+0x74`. A busy index table just clears that flag. The port is then
/// signalled with reason `0x13`.
